## Spectral frame and strengthened vacuum estimate

The physical coexact frame is `U=polar(K Q Lambda^-1)`. If
`V=K Q Lambda^-1`, the producer checks
`||V-Q||<=r/min(Lambda)` and `||V^T V-I||<=polar_error<1`.
The singular-value formula for polar decomposition gives
`||U-V||<=polar_error`, hence the stated `delta` bound for `||U-Q||`.
Then

    ||U^T K U-Lambda|| <= r+(||K||+max(Lambda))delta = eta_bound.

No rounded eigenvector is treated as exact. Vacuum perturbation, every free
interval, and every current-coordinate error remain separate. The fourth
Gaussian moment is bounded by
`v²[(4L²+190)²+16L²+380]`; this supplies the published quadratic Duhamel
