recomputes these exact rational upper bounds independently.

The published vacuum estimate is valid but can be strengthened without
changing any source, state preparation, or native word. Set

    C = U^T K U, lambda0 = min(Lambda)-eta > 0,
    W = sqrt((b/a) C), W0 = sqrt((b/a) Lambda),
    rho = eta/(2 lambda0) < 1.

The Sylvester equation for the difference of positive square roots, or its
convergent positive-semigroup integral, gives

    ||W-W0|| <= sqrt(b/a) eta/(2 sqrt(lambda0)).

Consequently the symmetric positive matrix
`R=W0^(-1/2) W W0^(-1/2)` obeys `||R-I||<=rho`. This does not require C and
Lambda to commute. For eigenvalues `r_j` of R, direct Gaussian integration
of the normalized positive real wavefunctions gives

    overlap² = product_j 2 sqrt(r_j)/(1+r_j),
    -log(overlap²) = sum_j log cosh(log(r_j)/2).

Using `log cosh(x)<=x²/2`, `|log(r_j)|<=rho/(1-rho)`, and
`2(1-exp(-x/2))<=x`, their norm difference satisfies

    ||Omega_C-Omega_Lambda||
       <= sqrt(190/8) rho/(1-rho).

The audit evaluates a rational outward square root for this formula. It
replaces only the old vacuum term in both one/two-macro complete-record
and Fourier-edge budgets. The other terms, including native failure and
